                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 3296,
                            "last_played": 1792719343
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There are so few well thought out video games that adapt Shakespeare, and Kreg Segall's A Midsummer Night's Choice is certainly one of them. The way that he effortlessly draws from a variety of Shakespeare's texts while also giving the player power and autonomy to shape the narrative themselves is really well balanced here. The game is also quite charming and hearkens back to the origins of text-based adventure games. A delight.",
